{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghqwPcd9aZcsCqUF3DBY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Setup.** The ground state is ³T₁(F). The observed bands are ³T₁(F)→³T₂ (17 500), ³T₁(F)→³T₁(P) (25 000) and ³T₁(F)→¹E (9 748). I write all energies relative to the ³F barycentre.\n\nI rebuilt the Tanabe–Sugano matrices from memory, so I checked each against its Dq = 0 limit.\n\n**³T₁ matrix** (basis t₂², t₂e):\n\n- Matrix: [[3B − 8Dq, 6B], [6B, 12B + 2Dq]]\n- Eigenvalues: E± = (15B − 6Dq)/2 ± √[((9B + 10Dq)/2)² + 36B²]\n- E₋ is the ground state and E₊ is ³T₁(P).\n- At Dq = 0 these reduce to 0 and 15B, as they should.\n\n**³T₂** lies at 2Dq. It is pure F and does not mix.\n\n**Solving for Dq and B**\n\n1. The ³T₁(P) − ³T₁(F) gap gives 2√[((9B + 10Dq)/2)² + 36B²] = 25 000.\n2. The ³T₂ − ³T₁(F) gap gives 2Dq − E₋ = 17 500. With the square root equal to 12 500 from step 1, this reduces to 5Dq − 7.5B = 5000, so Dq = 1000 + 1.5B.\n3. Substituting into step 1 gives 180B² + 120 000B − 1.3125×10⁸ = 0, so B ≈ 583 cm⁻¹.\n4. Then Dq = 1000 + 1.5(583.3) ≈ 1875 cm⁻¹.\n5. The ground state is E₋ = −13 750 cm⁻¹.\n\n**¹E matrix** (basis t₂², e²):\n\n- Matrix: [[9B + 2C − 8Dq, −2√3 B], [−2√3 B, 8B + 2C + 12Dq]]\n- At Dq = 0 the eigenvalues are ¹D = 5B + 2C and ¹G = 12B + 2C, as they should be.\n- With B = 583.3 and Dq = 1875, the diagonal entries are 2C − 9750 and 2C + 27 167.\n- The lower eigenvalue is 2C − 9860.\n\n**Solving for C**\n\nSetting (2C − 9860) − (−13 750) = 9748 gives 2C ≈ 5858, so C ≈ 2929 cm⁻¹. This gives C/B ≈ 5.0.\n\n**Result:** Dq ≈ 1875 cm⁻¹, B ≈ 583 cm⁻¹, C ≈ 2929 cm⁻¹.\n\n{\"Dq\": 1875, \"B\": 583, \"C\": 2929, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Dq and B follow from the two spin-allowed triplet bands via the 3T1 matrix, and C from the 1E band including t2^2/e^2 mixing.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_inp